docs/audits/phase-3-audit-result-v1.log:306:CLAUDE.md:36:Real, measured latency (M5 16GB, `Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507-4bit` + `whisper-small-mlx`): median ~3.2s, p95 ~3.8s from end-of-speech to first audio (`npm run bench:voice`, target was ≤4s/≤8s — met). Default TTS is `TTS_ENGINE=say` using `SAY_VOICE` (default `Felipe (Enhanced)`, not the compact `Luciana` voice from the original plan) — macOS's "Enhanced"/"Aprimorada" quality voices sound noticeably better than compact ones at the same ~0.5s latency, so there's no reason to use compact. `TTS_ENGINE=kokoro` (Kokoro-82M via the already-installed `~/.venvs/tts-say` venv, ~1.2s) remains available as an alternative but is not the default — the user compared compact `say`, `Luciana (Enhanced)`, `Felipe (Enhanced)`, and Kokoro on 2026-09-14 and picked `Felipe (Enhanced)`.
